  "worked_solution": "To plot $y=\\frac{3}{2x},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\frac{1}{x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831126/assets/a32495fcca947d01cf8d3218fc5cfc0cce083a34e6fb6b629d92ba9e47039a6e.png)\n\n- Stretch the result by a scale factor of $\\frac{3}{2}$ parallel to the $y$-axis to get the graph of $y=\\frac{3}{2x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13831126/assets/5a43656a35d47c7321e53d56238cd10f669bc807d57f72fcc002d79fb21aa111.png)",
